1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,018
Chapter 5. The betrayal.

2
00:00:03,318 --> 00:00:10,035
In the early nineties, Sony and Nintendo were working together on a CD drive for the Super Nintendo.

3
00:00:10,215 --> 00:00:15,271
In 1991, Nintendo announced it would build it… with Philips.

4
00:00:15,451 --> 00:00:21,564
At Sony, many wanted to move on. One engineer, Ken Kutaragi, did not.

5
00:00:21,744 --> 00:00:31,103
On December 3, 1994, Sony launched its own console in Japan. It used CDs. It bet everything on 3D.

6
00:00:31,283 --> 00:00:36,113
It was called PlayStation. It sold over 102 million units.

7
00:00:36,763 --> 00:00:41,291
Nintendo had lost a partner. And gained a rival.
